"[2604.15497v1] Endomorphisms of Hecke-Kiselman Monoids Associated to Simple Oriented Graphs (https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.15497v1)\nciteturn10172view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.15497v1\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 161\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Mathematics > Group Theory\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 16 Apr 2026 (this version), latest version 4 Aug 2026 (cite5†v3 )]\nL9: # Title:Endomorphisms of Hecke-Kiselman Monoids Associated to Simple Oriented Graphs\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Luka Andrenšek L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Endomorphisms of Hecke-Kiselman Monoids Associated to Simple Oriented Graphs, by Luka Andren\\v{s}ek\nL14: \nL15: cite7†View PDF cite8†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:Let $\\mathrm{HK}_{\\Theta}$ denote the Hecke-Kiselman monoid associated to a finite simple oriented graph $\\Theta$. We reduce the problem of describing the endomorphism monoid $\\mathrm{End}(\\mathrm{HK}_{\\Theta})$ to determining when a product of two idempotents in $\\mathrm{HK}_{\\Theta}$ is again an idempotent. This yields a procedure for constructing a Boolean matrix monoid isomorphic to $\\mathrm{End}(\\mathrm{HK}_{\\Theta})$.\nL17: As an application, we obtain an explicit description of the endomorphism monoid of the Catalan monoid $\\mathcal{C}_{n+1}$.\nL18: Comments:  | 14 pages\nL19: Subjects:  | Group Theory (math.GR)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:2604.15497 [math.GR]\nL21:    | (or cite10†arXiv:2604.15497v1 [math.GR] for this version)\nL22:    | cite11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2604.15497†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: ## Submission history\nL24: \nL25: From: Luka Andrenšek [cite12†view email ]\nL26: [